ent :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12{x}^{3}}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb221971-81aa-5b2d-a077-c6b670f32b1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298367} :answer-field/id #uuid "b39d87eb-5482-5669-84b6-1f25fa680a00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299244}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c5f8a50f-d033-5259-86d9-bade982764d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-32000" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=2\\operatorname{arccsc} (8-{x}^{4}).$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccsc} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc} \\,x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{arccsc} (8-{x}^{4})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc} (8-{x}^{4})) \\\\  & =2\\left(-\\frac{1}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8-{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =2\\left(-\\frac{1}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}}\\right)\\cdot (-4{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287924 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02d0cca3-b930-583a-a67f-b7d2fbb30dc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}(1+\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{2}))}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284811} {:answer/id #uuid "29fc1d7b-795e-5330-9fed-248e9bdfb72b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}(1+{\\operatorname{arcsec} }^{2}({x}^{2}))}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285156} {:answer/id #uuid "9615675e-d4e7-5987-b50d-4218c3a5988d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}(1+{\\operatorname{arcsec} }^{2}({x}^{2}))}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286150} {:answer/id #uuid "c54342e1-8752-5e65-99b0-9ee8dc40302a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}(1+{\\operatorname{arcsec} }^{2}({x}^{2}))}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286596} {:answer/id #uuid "d33e9472-db4f-5b53-bf24-f8efe37e24bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}(1-\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{2}))}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9615675e-d4e7-5987-b50d-4218c3a5988d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}(1+{\\operatorname{arcsec} }^{2}({x}^{2}))}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286150} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb52bc86-fbbc-58f3-a753-d854efd39ec9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287568}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7aebb99a-4bdf-525d-8f3e-1c1f2acc8b2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-19082" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{2})).$" :question/worked-solution "The formulae for the derivatives of $arctan$ and $\\operatorname{arcsec} $ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arctanx) & =\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} x) & =\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formulae above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{2}))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+(\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{2}))^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+(\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{2}))^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}|\\sqrt{({x}^{2})^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+(\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{2}))^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}|\\sqrt{({x}^{2})^{2}-1}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}(1+{\\operatorname{arcsec} }^{2}({x}^{2}))}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297337 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d9296d0-17e2-5a28-a674-eb8958050df1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d9296d0-17e2-5a28-a674-eb8958050df1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295344} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ddd26fa-15fe-5961-a3b9-0d7aba29d816" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296665}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "99fbb8d5-fc1d-5b4d-b999-a3255c91ff23" :question/math-academy-id "q-312364" :question/problem "Calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=5\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{2}+3)$ at $x=2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arcsec} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} \\,x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{2}+3)) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}+3|\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+3)^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+3) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}+3|\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+3)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{10x}{|{x}^{2}+3|\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+3)^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve at $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{10(2)}{|{2}^{2}+3|\\sqrt{({2}^{2}+3)^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{|7|\\sqrt{49-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{7\\sqrt{48}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{7\\cdot 4\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299712 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e6323d4-42fa-5b0a-a662-4875e0f19a7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297620} {:answer/id #uuid "1dfb3f79-ae92-53fa-8e4f-156ba3393900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297682} {:answer/id #uuid "4da0246a-281e-5bbd-b144-5324057a41ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297874} {:answer/id #uuid "76bb75f6-7ed6-57dd-8f7b-90731f1a1dd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298069} {:answer/id #uuid "e509e5c4-b769-5afd-a4b5-879400fecc6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dfb3f79-ae92-53fa-8e4f-156ba3393900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297682} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b7e2a43-6f12-5344-877a-8a1d3b75d45c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298673}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7013dfd6-3ee9-5a67-9438-689c7906b87e" :question/math-academy-id "q-31903" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent line to the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{3}-6x)$ at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arcsec} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} ({x}^{3}-6x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|{x}^{3}-6x|\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-6x)^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}-6x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|{x}^{3}-6x|\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-6x)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}-6}{|{x}^{3}-6x|\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-6x)^{2}-1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line to the curve at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(1)\\text{ } & =\\frac{3(1)^{2}-6}{|{1}^{3}-6(1)|\\sqrt{({1}^{3}-6(1))^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{|-5|\\sqrt{(1-6)^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{4\\cdot 6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\cdot \\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\cdot 2\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{10\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{10\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{60} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299772 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01348264-a81e-56c3-895f-616259a8e027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297556} {:answer/id #uuid "0394f679-9a1c-5b87-94ed-5055b0ccff99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297572} {:answer/id #uuid "50c36e45-828c-545f-9d7e-4d60c934349c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297888} {:answer/id #uuid "5a70b39e-a686-576d-b119-facfb9478e8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297932} {:answer/id #uuid "fe851005-bb92-50a4-8f77-18e97f095b87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0394f679-9a1c-5b87-94ed-5055b0ccff99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297572} :answer-field/id #uuid "29c39276-107a-53e2-88ed-bb72cf785946" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298779}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b0ce731-e82d-557a-b699-13d5ea673ea4" :question/math-academy-id "q-31951" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=2\\operatorname{arcsec} (6x-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arcsec} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{arcsec} (6x-1)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} (6x-1)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{(6x-1)^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x-1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{{(6x-1)}^{2}-1}}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-12x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{4(9{x}^{2}-3x)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315051 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d71143b0-47a4-55bc-833a-9a37cf1a0cb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d71143b0-47a4-55bc-833a-9a37cf1a0cb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313670} :answer-field/id #uuid "42df9230-a42a-5643-ac02-c0cf183c1ecb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314193}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7de810d1-79ef-5695-be73-3f0627f342f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-341115" :question/problem "Calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=\\operatorname{arcsec} ({e}^{x})$ at $x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡10.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arcsec} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} \\,x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arcsec} ({e}^{x})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|{e}^{x}|\\sqrt{{({e}^{x})}^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}-1}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve at $x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡10$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡10) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)/2)}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315052 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09524a5a-9f20-5efe-91fd-6d5a59158a20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09524a5a-9f20-5efe-91fd-6d5a59158a20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312043} :answer-field/id #uuid "066f745e-563a-5525-a0d9-6cba6aa1ca90" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314029}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f221de46-11bc-5772-aa56-5d0d13b544a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-341121" :question/problem "Calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=\\operatorname{arccsc} (\\sqrt{x})$ at $x=2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccsc} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc} \\,x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arccsc} (\\sqrt{x})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|\\sqrt{x}|\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}\\sqrt{x-1}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{x-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve at $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(2) & =-\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2-1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Chain Rule"}]}
